# noergler team self-service, IntelliJ HTTP client. Pick an environment
# (dev / prod): copy http-client.env.json.example to http-client.env.json (gitignored), fill in host, team, secret and
# token there; do not commit secret or token.
#   {{secret}}  the team's webhook secret (from the noergler admin): authenticates every call
#   {{token}}   your own Bitbucket HTTP access token with project admin: /onboard only,
#               NOT the bot's BITBUCKET_TOKEN (it has no admin)

### Claim a whole project and some repos of a shared one, create the hooks, grant the bot write access
POST {{host}}/onboard/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
X-Bitbucket-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "grant-bot",
  "projects": [
    {"key": "PLAT"},
    {"key": "INFRA", "repos": ["terraform-core", "ansible"]}
  ]
}

### Same, but only report what would happen (no claim, no hook, no grant)
POST {{host}}/onboard/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
X-Bitbucket-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "grant-bot",
  "dry_run": true,
  "projects": [{"key": "PLAT"}]
}

### Re-run the hooks over the current claims (after a webhook secret rotation: remove first, see below)
POST {{host}}/onboard/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
X-Bitbucket-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "grant-bot"}
